              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "moror, morārī — \"to delay, to linger; to hold up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Viātor in caupōnā nōn morātur, quod nox venit. The traveller does not linger at the inn, because night is coming."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Deponent: moror, morārī, morātus sum, from mora 'delay'. Nōlī morārī, don't hang about. English moratorium comes from the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "moror is built on mora 'delay' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), a regular first-conjugation deponent made from the noun."
            }
          ]
        },
